    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "To resolve this, we can integrate the heuristic routing directly into Inductor's scheduler and update the Triton lowering for the register-tiled path.\n\n1. Scheduler Heuristic\nWe can route the kernels based on the reduction dimension (N), using the crossover point observed in the data.\n\nPython\nimport torch\nfrom torch._inductor.utils import has_tma_support\n\ndef get_rmsnorm_strategy(M: int, N: int, dtype: torch.dtype):\n    if N <= 1024:\n        return \"standard_persistent\"\n    if N <= 8192:\n        return \"reg_tiled_fp16_cache\"\n    if N > 8192 and has_tma_support():\n        return \"tma_smem_cache\"\n    return \"multi_pass_reduction\"\n2. Triton Lowering (Register Tiled Path)\nFor the reg_tiled_fp16_cache, here is the generator logic to dynamically unroll loads and handle the on-the-fly fp32 casting:\n\nPython\ndef generate_reg_tiled_rmsnorm(V, N, unroll_factor=2):\n    lines = []\n    lines.append(f\"offs = tl.arange(0, {V.sym_tile})[None, :]\")\n    \n    for i in range(unroll_factor):\n        offset_str = f\" + {i} * {V.sym_tile}\" if i > 0 else \"\"\n        lines.append(f\"x{i} = tl.load(base + offs{offset_str}, mask=mask, other=0.0)\")\n        \n    lines.append(\"ss = tl.zeros([1, TILE], dtype=tl.float32)\")\n    for i in range(unroll_factor):\n        lines.append(f\"ss += x{i}.to(tl.float32) * x{i}.to(tl.float32)\")\n        \n    lines.append(f\"inv_rms = tl.rsqrt(tl.sum(ss, axis=1)[:, None] / ({unroll_factor} * TILE) + EPS)\")\n    \n    for i in range(unroll_factor):\n        offset_str = f\" + {i} * {V.sym_tile}\" if i > 0 else \"\"\n        lines.append(f\"w{i} = tl.load(w_ptr + offs{offset_str})\")\n        lines.append(f\"tl.store(ybase + offs{offset_str}, (x{i}.to(tl.float32) * inv_rms * w{i}).to({V.out_dtype}), mask=mask)\")\n        \n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\nResolution\nImplemented the dual-path optimization for persistent reductions. N <= 8192 routes to the fp16 register-tiled kernel for higher ILP, and N > 8192 routes to the TMA-smem kernel to bypass register pressure. Closing this issue.",
