    "body": "> Would you mind sharing a complete benchmark with your changes and comparisons ?\n\n1. Initial performance numbers posted in issue description (e.g. 97% SOL) is inflated. The original `benchmark_with_profiler` ran all trials inside a single `with profile()` block without an explicit `torch.cuda.synchronize()` between the L2 flush and the kernel launch. This meant some iterations hit warm L2 cache despite the flush attempt, understating kernel latency. Corrected in new [benchmark script](https://gist.github.com/liqiangxl/d97e6130966bcd3f046f2523e82086e5 )\n\n2. Measured on GB200 using [this branch](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/182671), RMSNorm (`x.pow(2).mean().rsqrt() * w`), bfloat16, peak BW=7928 GB/s.\n\n### Speedup (register-tiled / baseline)\n\n| M \\ N |  2048 |  4096 |  8192 | 16384 |\n|------:|------:|------:|------:|------:|\n|  2048 |  0.81 |  0.80 |  1.16 |  1.25 |\n|  4096 |  1.09 |  0.96 |  0.93 |  1.25 |\n|  8192 |  1.29 |  1.16 |  1.08 |  1.16 |\n| 16384 |  1.15 |  1.10 |  1.07 |  1.12 |\n| 32768 |  1.13 |  1.07 |  1.05 |  1.06 |\n\n### SOL% (baseline \u2192 register-tiled)\n\n| M \\ N |     2048 |     4096 |     8192 |    16384 |\n|------:|---------:|---------:|---------:|---------:|\n|  2048 | 50\u219241%   | 62\u219250%   | 67\u219278%   | 58\u219273%   |\n|  4096 | 62\u219267%   | 67\u219264%   | 76\u219271%   | 67\u219284%   |\n|  8192 | 66\u219285%   | 74\u219286%   | 82\u219288%   | 77\u219289%   |\n| 16384 | 73\u219284%   | 81\u219289%   | 85\u219291%   | 81\u219291%   |\n| 32768 | 78\u219289%   | 86\u219292%   | 88\u219292%   | 85\u219290%   |\n\n### Kernel Latency (us): baseline \u2192 register-tiled\n\n| M \\ N |        2048 |        4096 |        8192 |       16384 |\n|------:|------------:|------------:|------------:|------------:|\n|  2048 |   4.2\u21925.2   |   6.8\u21928.5   |  12.6\u219210.9  |  29.3\u219223.4  |\n|  4096 |   6.9\u21926.3   |  12.7\u219213.2  |  22.4\u219224.0  |  50.7\u219240.4  |\n|  8192 |  12.8\u21929.9   |  22.8\u219219.7  |  41.6\u219238.4  |  87.7\u219275.8  |\n| 16384 |  23.2\u219220.2  |  41.8\u219238.0  |  79.6\u219274.3  | 166.4\u2192148.6 |\n| 32768 |  43.3\u219238.2  |  78.6\u219273.8  | 154.3\u2192147.3 | 320.5\u2192301.3 |\n",
