    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "> Neat trick with the lower dtype in registers. I don't see any overlapping shapes comparing the baseline, the register optimization, and TMA? I think landing the register optimization would be viable, and I would suspect that TMA might not add too much on top of that?\n\nThanks for the feedback. TMA is still experimental. The idea is to use shared memory caching inputs to reduce register pressure.",
